 - Saved highlights stop at the selected text before a joined dash; the floating Edit/Delete toolbar has larger high-contrast icons. Highlights also continue across page breaks inside hyphenated words, without changing saved clipping text.

+- The EPUB contents index collapses parent chapters, opens the current chapter's ancestors, and supports holding a parent to navigate to it.
+
 - Highlights are grouped under collapsible chapter headers with counts; opening and deleting a highlight preserve its original identity.

 - Readest position sync translates original chapter coordinates through the optimizer source map when the cloud EPUB is unavailable; converted books without a map leave the device position unchanged.
@@ -301,6 +303,8 @@

 - Use right/down disclosure icons and indent highlight children. Tapping a clipping offers Open in book, Edit highlight and immediate Delete. The footer shows the full clipping count, current/total list pages and previous/next controls.

+- Use right/down disclosure icons with geometric child indentation in the nested chapter index.
+
 ## [v1.6.0] - 2026-09-21

 ### Added
@@ -810,4 +814,5 @@
 - Start touch word selection after a 200 ms stationary hold instead of one second; immediate swipes remain page turns.
 - Save dragged multiword highlights immediately on release, and open saved quote controls without a flashing refresh.
 - Keep highlight drags attached through brief contact gaps and between words/lines; defer idle SD preparation during page swipes.
+- Keep chapter headings bold, including normal-weight publisher spans, and use bold chapter labels in navigation.
 - Use Yellow, Green, Red, and Blue highlights with evenly stepped grayscale swatches, named filters, matching Readest colors, and stable saved IDs. Removed Orange highlights and defaults map to Yellow; Red retains contrasting text.
